01_steane_ghz_cpu.ipynb is adapted from "How to use PennyLane and Backline for
low-latency quantum error correction on GPUs and FPGAs" by Josh Izaac, Mehrdad Malek,
Joseph Lee and Kalman Szenes (https://pennylane.ai/demos/backline).

Changes made by qBraid:
- Kept only the local CPU-to-CPU section; the remote GPU and FPGA sections are left out.
- Loads the Steane decoder library from the installed Catalyst package instead of a
  Catalyst source build.
- Added a setup check, a two-logical-qubit run before the original three-qubit run,
  timings, and short explanations.
